title: A Faction Breaks Away
subtitle: A faction's quarrel with the leadership ends in a split.
new-page: true
tags: rf_event
view-if: split_pending = 1 and rf_over = 0
on-arrival: {!
var f = Q.split_faction;
Q.split_name = window.RF.names[f];
Q.members -= Math.round(Q[f + '_strength'] * 1.2);
Q.union_influence -= 4;
Q[f + '_expelled'] = 1;
Q.split_pending = 0;
window.RF.normalize(Q);
!}

= The [+ split_name +] leaves the party

The leadership has had enough, and so has the [+ split_name +]. Its leaders are expelled for factional activity, and a share of the membership follows them out. They will form a small group of their own, as the KAPD did in 1920 and as the KPO and the Leninbund would later.
